This provision is important because it ensures that the Commission, as the EU's executive body, is accountable to the member states and that the member states have a say in the exercise of the Commission's powers. It also helps to ensure that the Commission acts in the best interests of the EU as a whole, rather than solely in the interests of any one member state.
